# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git's core.autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For most text
# files that is harmless, but not for these:
#
#   *.patch  git apply matches context byte for byte. A CRLF rewrite makes every
#            hunk fail with "patch does not apply". Marked -text so Git stores and
#            restores the exact bytes.
#   *.sh     CRLF makes the shebang line unfindable on Linux/macOS: the kernel
#            then tries to exec /bin/bash\r, which does not exist.
#
# Everything else is normalised to LF in the repository and left alone on checkout.

* text=auto

*.patch -text
*.sh    text eol=lf

*.c     text
*.h     text
*.md    text
*.py    text
*.ps1   text
*.txt   text
*.csv   text
